#: chaotic_pfc.comms.metrics:1 of
msgid "Error metrics for the chaotic communication experiments."
msgstr "Error metrics for the chaotic communication experiments."



#: chaotic_pfc.comms.metrics:3 of
msgid ""
"The band-limited channel is a linear-phase FIR filter, so it delays the "
"received signal by its group delay ``(N_taps - 1) / 2`` samples. The "
"recovered message is therefore compared against the original message "
"after removing that known delay, otherwise the misalignment dominates the"
" error metrics (and, for a ±1 message, the sign error sits near 0.5 "
"regardless of the true quality of the recovery)."
msgstr ""
"The band-limited channel is a linear-phase FIR filter, so it delays the "
"received signal by its group delay ``(N_taps - 1) / 2`` samples. The "
"recovered message is therefore compared against the original message "
"after removing that known delay, otherwise the misalignment dominates the"
" error metrics (and, for a ±1 message, the sign error sits near 0.5 "
"regardless of the true quality of the recovery)."



#: chaotic_pfc.comms.metrics:10 of
msgid ""
"Nothing here changes the transmitter, the channel or the receiver: this "
"module only aligns the two signals before measuring."
msgstr ""
"Nothing here changes the transmitter, the channel or the receiver: this "
"module only aligns the two signals before measuring."



