#: ../../api/generated/chaotic_pfc.comms.metrics.rst:19:<autosummary>:1
#: chaotic_pfc.comms.metrics.DelayEstimate:1 of
msgid "Cross-correlation delay estimate between ``m`` and ``m_hat``."
msgstr "Cross-correlation delay estimate between ``m`` and ``m_hat``."



#: chaotic_pfc.comms.metrics.estimate_delay:3 of
msgid ""
"Lags from 0 to *max_lag* are scanned; the returned ``lag`` maximises "
"``|corr|``. The sign of ``corr_at_lag`` is reported so that a polarity "
"inversion is not mistaken for a delay."
msgstr ""
"Lags from 0 to *max_lag* are scanned; the returned ``lag`` maximises "
"``|corr|``. The sign of ``corr_at_lag`` is reported so that a polarity "
"inversion is not mistaken for a delay."



#: chaotic_pfc.comms.metrics.estimate_delay:7 of
msgid ""
"Note that when the recovery fails (``corr_at_lag`` is near zero, as in a "
"band-limited channel with no feedback filter), the argmax lag fits noise "
"and drifts with the record length; the lag is only meaningful once there "
"is a signal to correlate against. Callers should treat a small "
"``corr_at_lag`` as \"no delay estimate\", not as a measurement."
msgstr ""
"Note that when the recovery fails (``corr_at_lag`` is near zero, as in a "
"band-limited channel with no feedback filter), the argmax lag fits noise "
"and drifts with the record length; the lag is only meaningful once there "
"is a signal to correlate against. Callers should treat a small "
"``corr_at_lag`` as \"no delay estimate\", not as a measurement."



